  "flavor_text": {
    "one_line": "Fierce twilight elves who prize self-making, swift revenge, and beauty sharpened by danger.",
    "one_paragraph": "The Zhyssarel range through drowned forests and thorn-choked canopy roads where names are earned, discarded, and earned again. They distrust walls, fixed ranks, and every promise that lasts longer than desire, yet they keep memory through song, scars, and living trees grown around the ashes of honored dead. To them, beauty is not peace but intensity: the flash of a blade, a poisonous bloom, or a dance performed over a perilous drop."
